WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:18.400
One very important thing in search: if the user types a query, searches, and sees that there are no results related to it, there's a high risk they leave the website.

2
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:31.100
So here I need to try to keep the user on my website, to help them, so they don't lose hope and leave right away just because they found nothing related to their query.

3
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:51.700
So let's think about what to do when there are no search results. The most important guideline for a no-results page is to tell the user clearly that there are no results, so they understand it right away and don't keep looking.

4
00:00:51.700 --> 00:01:16.200
In this example the screen has a lot going on and gives it a strong hierarchy, but the message that there are no results is small, up at the top, so the user doesn't notice it and doesn't realize right away that there are none.

5
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.500
The user has to understand immediately that there are no results for exactly the query they wrote.

6
00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:41.200
Second: I don't block the user; I offer another path. I suggest edits to the query itself, or things close to what they wrote that may return results, or a different way of phrasing it they hadn't thought of.

7
00:01:41.200 --> 00:02:06.500
So they see the suggestions, pick one, and get results. I can also give them a button to go back: cancel the search, browse the whole website, or return to the home page or the page before the search.

8
00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:17.200
I offer other ways so the user doesn't feel they searched, found nothing, and have nothing left to do, so they leave and get no value from the product.

9
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:42.500
Third: I don't joke or make fun of the user. Humor at these moments can backfire: the user may leave the website, get annoyed by the joke and not come back, or find it silly.

10
00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:49.800
When the user is failing at a goal, we don't need to joke or sound sarcastic.

11
00:02:49.800 --> 00:03:12.800
Let's look at this example, which is a great search example with all the guidelines we covered. It's clear there are no search results, the page has a good hierarchy, and there are suggestions below.

12
00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:31.800
They can edit the query, check the spelling, try more general words or fewer words, and there are suggested queries to tap to see their results, with no sarcasm anywhere. So this is an excellent example that applies every guideline we discussed for the no-results page.
